## Key Takeaways

- Linux is the **kernel**; a **distribution** turns it into a complete operating system.
- Open source is the reason Linux is so widely used, adaptable and trusted.
- The command line is the main tool for working with Linux, especially on servers and in the cloud.
- Knowing which distribution family I'm on tells me which package manager to use.
- Practising commands hands-on made the concepts stick far better than reading alone.

